From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: xilinx: map OV2640 DVP UYVY to V4L2 UYVY

The OV2640 reports UYVY over its 8-bit parallel bus as two cycles per pixel.
The Xilinx VIPP format table only listed the packed 16-bit-per-cycle bus code,
so the capture node could not enumerate the sensor's default format.

---
 drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-vip.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-vip.c b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-vip.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-vip.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-vip.c
@@ -47,5 +47,8 @@ static const struct xvip_video_format xvip_video_formats[] = {
 	{ XVIP_VF_YUV_422, 8, NULL, MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYVY8_1X16,
 	  2, 16, V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUYV, 1, 1, 2, 1 },
 	{ XVIP_VF_VUY_422, 8, NULL, MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYVY8_1X16,
 	  2, 16, V4L2_PIX_FMT_UYVY, 1, 1, 2, 1 },
+	/* OV2640's 8-bit DVP output sends each UYVY pixel over two cycles. */
+	{ XVIP_VF_VUY_422, 8, NULL, MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYVY8_2X8,
+	  2, 16, V4L2_PIX_FMT_UYVY, 1, 1, 2, 1 },
 	{ XVIP_VF_YUV_422, 10, NULL, MEDIA_BUS_FMT_UYVY10_1X20,
 	  1, 16, V4L2_PIX_FMT_XV20, 2, 1, 2, 1 },
-- 
